        "full-FOL, standpoint/world/time-indexed, and aggregate-comparison (COUNT/SUM threshold) integrity conditions exceed that fragment; there is no formula-level aggregate term, so an aggregate comparison cannot be expressed as a genuine GROUP BY sub-SELECT and is carried-and-flagged, not projected" ,
        "the projectable fragment is a range-restricted, ∀-guarded integrity condition (guard(this) → φ(this)) whose per-focus condition φ is a Horn / NNF tree of binary atoms, existentials, disjunctions and (path-)universals: it lowers to a SELECT $this WHERE { guard ∧ ¬φ } via BGP + FILTER NOT EXISTS + UNION" ,
        "the surface is emit-only: there is no parse-back from a sh:SPARQLConstraint into a logic:Constraint (the logic: canon is the authoring ground, Principle 4)" ;
    logic:complexityClass "closed-world SPARQL constraint (SHACL Core)" ;
    logic:preservationKind logic:ValidationOnly .

<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/projection-ceiling:ceilings>
    a logic:ProjectionTarget ;
    rdfs:label "projection-ceiling:ceilings" ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "actual: projection-ceiling projection 'projection-ceiling:ceilings' is a sound under-approximation: every emitted row is entailed by its gmeow:ProjectionCeilingCommitment individual; the reifier identity and annotation coat are the enumerated residue (derived preservation = logic:SoundUnderApproximation)" ,
        "the gmeow:ProjectionCeilingCommitment annotation coat (any rationale / provenance triples on the individual) is dropped: the TSV projects only the core tuple" ,
        "the reified gmeow:ProjectionCeilingCommitment subject identity (the individual IRI) is dropped: the TSV row carries only the projected tuple, not its reifier" ;
    logic:complexityClass "n/a" ;
    logic:preservationKind logic:SoundUnderApproximation .

