        "actual: reasoning contract (preset logic:StratifiedNAFProfile) is not representable in SHACL-AF; the full facet selection is dropped (preserved only in the canonical RDF 1.2 projection)" ,
        "actual: reasoning contract (preset logic:WellFoundedProfile) is not representable in SHACL-AF; the full facet selection is dropped (preserved only in the canonical RDF 1.2 projection)" ,
        "ground class/property subsumption axioms are projected as cax-sco / prp-spo1 sh:SPARQLRule shapes; every other ground axiom (type / metamodel assertions, asserted relations, domain/range, modal or scoped axioms, literal-valued assertions) is not a derivation rule, has no SHACL-AF form, and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer (recorded as a drop)" ,
        "modal / world / standpoint context of a contextualized rule has no SHACL-AF form; a context-scoped rule is not projected (it would be unsound over the default graph) and is recorded as a drop" ,
        "the SHACL-AF surface is emit-only: there is no parse-back from sh:SPARQLRule into a logic: rule (the logic: canon is the authoring ground, Principle 4)" ,
        "the stratified Horn-with-stratified-negation-and-aggregation rule fragment is projected (positive body → graph patterns, negation-as-failure → FILTER NOT EXISTS, inequality guards → FILTER, and a reduce rule → an aggregating sh:SPARQLRule with a GROUP-BY sub-SELECT): full first-order formula bodies, existential (value-inventing) rule heads, and ground-subject rules have no faithful SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule form and remain in the canonical logic: layer (carried by canonical-rdf12)" ;
    logic:complexityClass "terminating/PTIME-data" ;
    logic:preservationKind logic:SoundUnderApproximation .

<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-core>
    a logic:ProjectionTarget ;
    rdfs:label "shacl-core" ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "a shape surface validates but does not entail (ValidationOnly)" ,
        "actual: datetime validity pattern (yyyy-mm-ddTHH:MM:SS) on https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/openehr/testdatatypes/value is a format template, not an XPath regex; it has no faithful SHACL/ShEx form (emitting it as sh:pattern would reject every valid datetime), so its meaning is carried in the canonical logic: layer" ,
        "actual: ordinal set on https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/openehr/testdatatypes/value projects only its coded symbols (sh:in); the ordinal integer values (1, 2, 3) and their ordering have no SHACL/ShEx form and are carried in the canonical logic: layer" ,
        "actual: sh:pattern on https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/bic carries regex-dialect residue (SHACL uses the XPath regular-expression flavour; the source dialect may differ): ^[A-Z]{6}[A-Z0-9]{2}([A-Z0-9]{3})?$" ,
        "actual: sh:pattern on https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/openehr/bloodpressure/text carries regex-dialect residue (SHACL uses the XPath regular-expression flavour; the source dialect may differ): .*" ,
        "actual: sh:pattern on https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/openehr/bloodpressure/text carries regex-dialect residue (SHACL uses the XPath regular-expression flavour; the source dialect may differ): openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER\\.anatomical_location(-[a-zA-Z0-9_]+)*\\.v1" ,
        "actual: sh:pattern on https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/openehr/bloodpressure/text carries regex-dialect residue (SHACL uses the XPath regular-expression flavour; the source dialect may differ): openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER\\.device(-[a-zA-Z0-9_]+)*\\.v1" ,
        "actual: sh:pattern on https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/openehr/bloodpressure/text carries regex-dialect residue (SHACL uses the XPath regular-expression flavour; the source dialect may differ): openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER\\.level_of_exertion(-[a-zA-Z0-9_]+)*\\.v1" ,
        "actual: sh:pattern on https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/openehr/testdatatypes/text carries regex-dialect residue (SHACL uses the XPath regular-expression flavour; the source dialect may differ): assignerC" ,
        "actual: sh:pattern on https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/openehr/testdatatypes/text carries regex-dialect residue (SHACL uses the XPath regular-expression flavour; the source dialect may differ): issuerA" ,
        "actual: sh:pattern on https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/openehr/testdatatypes/text carries regex-dialect residue (SHACL uses the XPath regular-expression flavour; the source dialect may differ): typeB" ,
        "actual: terminology binding on https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/openehr/bloodpressure/termBinding to SNOMED-CT (4 code(s)) has no faithful SHACL Core form; carried in the canonical logic: layer" ,
        "an intentionally-open existential range (owl:someValuesFrom owl:Thing / rdfs:Literal) is read closed-world as a bare sh:nodeKind (sh:BlankNodeOrIRI / sh:Literal): the existential's at-least-one force and the vacuous universal-top class membership are dropped, and the open range is carried in the canonical logic: layer" ,
        "full-FOL integrity conditions, standpoint/world/time-indexed constraints, and cross-node conditions have no SHACL Core form and are carried in the canonical logic: layer" ,
        "sh:pattern carries regex-dialect residue (SHACL uses the XPath flavour) and external terminology bindings have no faithful SHACL Core form; both are carried and flagged per shape" ;
    logic:complexityClass "closed-world shape validation (SHACL Core)" ;
    logic:preservationKind logic:ValidationOnly .

